The mismatch is happening because the two files are looking for the category property using different naming conventions (camelCase vs. UPPERCASE).
When you select a voucher in the main table, the backend passes the object with camelCase properties (e.g., categoryName).
 * In **Manual** (VoucherPosting.js), you correctly look for selectedVoucher.categoryName.
 * In **Bulk** (VoucherBulkUpload.js), the code is incorrectly looking for selectedVoucher.CATEGORY_NAME or selectedVoucher.category, which are both undefined, causing it to fall back to the default "General".
Here is the exact fix to make them match perfectly.
### The Fix: Update VoucherBulkUpload.js
Open VoucherBulkUpload.js and scroll down to the STANDARDIZED HORIZONTAL SELECTION HEADER section where the selectedVoucher details are displayed.
**Find this exact block of code:**
```javascript
                <Box>
                  <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>Category</Typography>
                  <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="500">{selectedVoucher.CATEGORY_NAME || selectedVoucher.category || "General"}</Typography>
                </Box>

```
**Replace it completely with this:**
```javascript
                <Box>
                  <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>Category</Typography>
                  <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="500">{selectedVoucher.categoryName || "General"}</Typography>
                </Box>

```
By changing it to selectedVoucher.categoryName, the Bulk component will now read the exact same property that the Manual component reads, perfectly resolving the discrepancy!
